Syntax: infuse <item> <essence>

Infuse writes what an essence holds onto a piece of gear.

The essence's quality is what it writes, and the whole essence is spent
however little of it lands -- so grow one to exactly the size you need and
never overshoot.

A piece holds three stats at most.  The first may reach five, the second
four, the third three, and a fourth will not go on at all.  The essence
costs the same wherever you put it, so a piece that concentrates on one
thing beats a piece spread across three.

Writing over a stat already there only ever raises it.  An essence that
would match it or fall short is refused rather than wasted.

Hit points, mana and movement are written in blocks of five and do not count
against the three.

See also: DISTILL, ESSENCE, BOLSTER
